From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: X7 Game build <x7game@invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: hichip: check that the nzclk CPU clock limit applied
 (X7 Game)

X7 Game boots with nzclk=900 because the FPU corrupts stores at the
factory 1188 MHz. The hook that applies it only logged the outcome at
KERN_INFO, which loglevel=5 hides, and never compared the rate read back
with the request. If the switch fails (clk_set_rate() error, or a read-back
that differs), print a KERN_EMERG line, which reaches the screen, and set
TAINT_CPU_OUT_OF_SPEC (bit 2 of /proc/sys/kernel/tainted) so user space
can check for it. Nothing changes when the switch works.

A bare "nzclk" or "nzc7" token (no '=') reached the handlers as NULL and
was passed to kstrtouint(), a NULL dereference long before any console
exists. Both handlers now return -EINVAL for a missing or unparsable
value, so do_early_param() prints "Malformed early option" instead.

The header comment promised "Raising the clock is refused", which the
code never did: it only accepts the four listed rates, all below
1188 MHz. Say that instead.
---
 arch/mips/generic/nzeus-fpudiag.c | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/generic/nzeus-fpudiag.c b/arch/mips/generic/nzeus-fpudiag.c
index e27cbe32c..35cc8b4e8 100644
--- a/arch/mips/generic/nzeus-fpudiag.c
+++ b/arch/mips/generic/nzeus-fpudiag.c
@@ -12,7 +12,13 @@
  *                Applied in plat_time_init() BEFORE the CP0 timer rate is
  *                read, through the existing hc16xx clock driver (the same
  *                MCPU select field the stock HiChip 4.4 kernel writes in
- *                hc16xx_set_cpu_clk). Raising the clock is refused.
+ *                hc16xx_set_cpu_clk). Only these four rates, all below the
+ *                factory 1188 MHz, are accepted; the rate is set whatever
+ *                the CPU ran at before. X7 Game always asks for 900 MHz
+ *                (the FPU corrupts stores at 1188 MHz): if the rate read
+ *                back is not the one asked for, a KERN_EMERG line is
+ *                printed and the kernel is tainted (TAINT_CPU_OUT_OF_SPEC,
+ *                bit 2 of /proc/sys/kernel/tainted).
  *   nzc7=<hex>   OR documented Config7 pipeline-control bits into Config7:
  *                CP1IO (6), SG (22), IALU (24), IAGN (25) only. Any other
  *                bit makes the whole value be ignored.
@@ -21,6 +27,7 @@
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/panic.h>
 #include <linux/printk.h>
 
 #include <asm/addrspace.h>
@@ -45,8 +52,14 @@ static int __init nz_clk_param(char *s)
 {
 	unsigned int mhz;
 
+	/*
+	 * A bare "nzclk" (no '=') arrives as NULL. A non-zero return makes
+	 * do_early_param() print "Malformed early option".
+	 */
+	if (!s)
+		return -EINVAL;
 	if (kstrtouint(s, 10, &mhz))
-		return 0;
+		return -EINVAL;
 	/* Only rates that exist in the clock table AND are below 1188 MHz. */
 	if (mhz == 297 || mhz == 396 || mhz == 594 || mhz == 900)
 		nz_clk_mhz = mhz;
@@ -60,8 +73,10 @@ static int __init nz_c7_param(char *s)
 {
 	unsigned int mask;
 
+	if (!s)
+		return -EINVAL;
 	if (kstrtouint(s, 16, &mask))
-		return 0;
+		return -EINVAL;
 	if (mask & ~NZ_C7_ALLOWED)
 		pr_warn("NZEUS_FPUDIAG nzc7=%#x refused (allowed bits %#x)\n",
 			mask, NZ_C7_ALLOWED);
@@ -112,9 +127,22 @@ void __init nzeus_fpudiag_early(struct clk *cpu_clk)
 	if (nz_clk_mhz && cpu_clk) {
 		unsigned long before = clk_get_rate(cpu_clk);
 		int ret = clk_set_rate(cpu_clk, nz_clk_mhz * 1000000UL);
+		unsigned long after = clk_get_rate(cpu_clk);
 
 		pr_info("NZEUS_FPUDIAG nzclk: %lu -> %lu Hz (request %u MHz, ret %d)\n",
-			before, clk_get_rate(cpu_clk), nz_clk_mhz, ret);
+			before, after, nz_clk_mhz, ret);
+
+		/*
+		 * X7 Game depends on this limit (see the top of this file). The
+		 * line above is KERN_INFO and hidden by loglevel=5, so a failed
+		 * switch is reported at KERN_EMERG, which reaches the screen, and
+		 * taints the kernel so user space can check for it.
+		 */
+		if (ret || after != nz_clk_mhz * 1000000UL) {
+			pr_emerg("X7: CPU clock limit %u MHz NOT applied (ret %d, now %lu Hz): FPU stores unreliable\n",
+				 nz_clk_mhz, ret, after);
+			add_taint(TAINT_CPU_OUT_OF_SPEC, LOCKDEP_STILL_OK);
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (nz_c7_mask) {
